@startuml
' Behavior 1 (Figure 4): normal publish -> acknowledge -> fan-out -> subscriber cursor.
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: behavior, publish, acknowledge, fan-out

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 230

participant "POS system" as POS #6FA8DC
participant "POS Adapter" as POSAD #6FA8DC
participant "Store Agent" as SA #93C47D
database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #8E7CC3
queue "Outbox" as OB #8E7CC3
participant "Communications\nFront-End" as CFE #F1C232
database "CFE event store" as CFEDB #8E7CC3
participant "Subscribers\n(CMI, Shipping-Order Fulfillment,\nStore-Tracking, Reporting, Analytics)" as SUB #F1C232

POS -> POSAD : sales record (event stream)
POSAD -> SA : Inventory Event
group one local step
  SA -> SLI : apply (update stock)
  SA -> OB : append (durable, ordered)
end
OB -> CFE : publish (Inventory Event)\nIEP / TLS 1.3 mutual certs [secure]
CFE -> CFEDB : persist (retain for replay)
CFE --> OB : acknowledge (acceptedThrough sequence)\n[secure]
note over OB : holds the last acknowledged\nsequence; acknowledged events\nmay then be pruned
CFE -> SUB : notify (every subscriber receives\nevery event and filters locally)
SUB --> CFE : acknowledge (applied through\nsequence N per source)
note over CFE, CFEDB : the CFE keeps a per-subscription delivered position; the event\nstore retains each accepted event until every subscription has\nacknowledged past it plus a retention window
note over SUB : idempotent by event ID;\nduplicates are ignored

note over SA, CFE : A store-raised Shipping Order travels as a second message type on\nthe same connector: the Store Agent raises it when a product reaches its\nminimum, the store manager confirms it, and it is published, acknowledged\nand fanned out exactly as above; Shipping-Order Fulfillment receives it and\nthe DC Agent publishes the DC-side stock event when the goods ship.

legend right
  Normal path. The store never blocks on the WAN:
  the local step completes first, then the Outbox
  publishes. At-least-once delivery, acknowledged
  per source sequence; subscribers acknowledge a
  cumulative cursor so the event store knows what
  it may release.
endlegend
@enduml
